{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">TERMINAL statement</span>\n","class":"manual","created":2879,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/310814","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/TERMINAL-statement.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/TERMINAL-statement.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"TERMINAL-statement\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">TERMINAL statement</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Changes terminal type during program execution.\nOn UNIX, changes the value of the TERM environment variable. </p>\n      <div class=\"note note note_note\"><span class=\"note__title\">Note:</span> Does not apply to SpeedScript programming.</div>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"TERMINAL-statement__syntax_GC1B1B22704967\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d346845e99\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"TERMINAL-statement__idGDP3062677344\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>TERMINAL = <var class=\"keyword varname\">termid</var></code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <dl class=\"dl parml\">\n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">termid</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">\n            <p class=\"p\">A terminal type string. The <var class=\"keyword varname\">termid</var> can also\nbe an expression. The AVM returns an error message if <var class=\"keyword varname\">termid</var> is\nnot defined in the PROTERMCAP file. However, <var class=\"keyword varname\">termid</var> can\nbe the word TERMINAL. The line TERMINAL=TERMINAL reinitializes the terminal.</p>\n          </dd>\n        \n      </dl>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"TERMINAL-statement__example_GC1B1B32704973\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d346845e154\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">This\nprocedure changes the terminal screen width from 80 columns to 132 columns,\nthen back again:</p>\n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <strong class=\"ph b\">r-seterm.p</strong>\n      </p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"TERMINAL-statement__idGDP3082677350\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>FOR EACH Customer NO-LOCK:\n  DISPLAY Customer.\nEND.\n\n<strong class=\"ph b\">TERMINAL = &quot;wy60w&quot;.</strong>\nOUTPUT TO TERMINAL PAGED.\nFOR EACH Customer NO-LOCK:\n  DISPLAY Customer WITH WIDTH 132.\nEND.\n\nOUTPUT CLOSE.\n<strong class=\"ph b\">TERMINAL = &quot;wy60&quot;.</strong>\nDISPLAY &quot;Back to 80 columns.&quot; WITH CENTERED.</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"TERMINAL-statement__notes_GC1B1B42704980\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d346845e195\">Notes</h2>\n      \n      <ul class=\"ul\">\n        <li class=\"li\">TERMINAL\ndoes not change the physical characteristics of a terminal. You\nmust supply a valid terminal type for the existing terminal state.</li>\n        <li class=\"li\">The TERMINAL statement reinitializes the function key definitions based\non the specified PROTERMCAP entry. If you have used ON statements\nto change function key definitions, the TERMINAL statement overrides\nthose changes.</li>\n        <li class=\"li\">If a subprocedure uses a frame, the frame is composed with the\nwidth that was in effect when the subprocedure was compiled. Changing\nthe width (terminal type) outside the scope of that procedure will\nnot change the frame width inside the procedure unless it is recompiled. <p class=\"p\">The\nfollowing sequence of statements does not work as intended, because <span class=\"ph filepath\">subp.p</span> is\nnot recompiled before its second execution:</p></li>\n      </ul>\n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <strong class=\"ph b\">r-setrm1.p</strong>\n      </p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"TERMINAL-statement__idGDP3092677357\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code><strong class=\"ph b\">TERMINAL = &quot;wy60w&quot;.</strong>\nRUN subp.p.\n\n<strong class=\"ph b\">TERMINAL = &quot;wy60&quot;.</strong>\nRUN subp.p.\n\nDISPLAY &quot;Frame (132) too big for screen (80)&quot; WITH CENTERED.</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"TERMINAL-statement__see-also_GC1B1B52704989\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d346845e249\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"TERMINAL-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/TERMINAL-function.html#TERMINAL-function\">TERMINAL function</a>\n      </p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"TERMINAL-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/TERMINAL-function.html\">TERMINAL function</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"THIS-OBJECT-statement.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/THIS-OBJECT-statement.html\">THIS-OBJECT statement</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/310814","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":2879,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"TERMINAL statement","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/TERMINAL-statement.html","type":"Manual"}